{
  "name": "Lead Generator v3 — Telegram + Gemini + Serper.dev",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚙️ One-time Setup\n\n**1. Telegram Bot**\n- Message @BotFather on Telegram → `/newbot` → follow prompts → copy the token\n- In n8n → Credentials → New → **Telegram API** → paste token\n- Bind the credential on both `Telegram Trigger` and `Send Acknowledgment` / `Send Results` nodes\n\n**2. Google Gemini API**\n- Get key from [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com) → API Keys\n- In n8n → Credentials → New → **Google Gemini(PaLM) API** → paste key\n- Bind the credential on the `Gemini Chat Model` sub-node\n\n**3. Serper.dev API**\n- Sign up at [serper.dev](https://serper.dev) → copy API key\n- In n8n → Credentials → New → **Header Auth** → Header Name: `X-API-KEY` → Header Value: your key\n- Bind on `Search Google Maps via Serper` node\n\n**4. How to trigger**\nSend your bot a message like:\n`electronics in Los Angeles`\n`dentists in New York`\n`restaurants in Lagos`\n\n**⚠️ Note:** The workflow must be **Active** (toggle in top-right) to receive Telegram messages. Test mode only fires when you manually execute.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Setup Instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [-160, -80],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔄 How This Works\n\n1. **Telegram Trigger** receives your message (e.g. \"dentists in New York\")\n2. **Acknowledgment** is sent immediately so you know it's working\n3. **Gemini Agent** extracts the keyword + location and generates 3 neighbourhood-level search queries\n4. **Parse Queries** converts the AI's JSON output into workflow items\n5. **Serper.dev** searches Google Maps for each query → returns business websites\n6. **Email scraper** fetches each website and regex-extracts email addresses\n7. **Results** (deduplicated, spam-filtered) are sent back to you via Telegram",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0002-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Architecture Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [540, -80],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": ["message"],
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0003-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Telegram Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "position": [240, 360],
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "webhookId": "lead-gen-v3-webhook-001",
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Telegram Bot API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{ $json.message.chat.id }}",
        "text": "=🔍 Processing your request for *{{ $json.message.text }}*...\n\nSearching 3 sub-areas across Google Maps. This usually takes 1-2 minutes.",
        "additionalFields": {
          "parseMode": "Markdown"
        }
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0004-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Send Acknowledgment",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "position": [480, 160],
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Telegram Bot API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "agentType": "conversationalAgent",
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.message.text }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a lead generation assistant.\n\nThe user sends a message like \"electronics in Los Angeles\" or \"dentists in New York\".\n\nYour job:\n1. Extract the keyword (e.g. \"electronics\") and the location (e.g. \"Los Angeles\")\n2. Generate exactly 3 search queries for real sub-areas/micro-neighbourhoods of that location\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array — no explanation, no markdown code blocks, no extra text:\n[{\"query\":\"neighbourhood+keyword\"},{\"query\":\"area+keyword\"},...]\n\nRules:\n- Replace spaces with + in query values\n- Place the keyword at the END of each query string\n- Use real, distinct neighbourhoods/districts of the given city\n- Generate exactly 3 items"
        }
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0005-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "AI Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "position": [480, 420],
      "typeVersion": 1.8
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelName": "models/gemini-2.0-flash",
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.2
        }
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0006-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Gemini Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
      "position": [480, 620],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "credentials": {
        "googlePalmApi": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Google Gemini API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "// The AI agent returns its response in $json.output\nconst raw = ($input.first().json.output || '').trim()\n\n// Strip markdown code fences if the model wraps in ```json ... ```\nconst cleaned = raw\n  .replace(/^```json\\s*/i, '')\n  .replace(/^```\\s*/i, '')\n  .replace(/```\\s*$/i, '')\n  .trim()\n\n// Extract the JSON array from the cleaned output\nconst match = cleaned.match(/\\[[\\s\\S]*\\]/)\nif (!match) {\n  // Fallback: return empty so pipeline gracefully produces 0 results\n  return []\n}\n\nlet queries\ntry {\n  queries = JSON.parse(match[0])\n} catch (e) {\n  return []\n}\n\nif (!Array.isArray(queries)) return []\n\n// Normalise: each item must have a { query: \"...\" } shape\nreturn queries\n  .filter(q => q && (typeof q === 'string' || typeof q.query === 'string'))\n  .map(q => ({ json: { query: typeof q === 'string' ? q : q.query } }))\n"
      },
      "id": "aaaaaaaa-0007-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Parse Queries from Agent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [720, 420],
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
